        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Astor, Florida; St. Johns River; Florida\n- Systems: Astor Bridge; State Road 40\n- Concepts: single-leaf bascule bridge; river length; commercial and recreational use; counties\n\nFacts:\n- The St. Johns River is the longest river in the U.S. state of Florida and is the state's most significant river for commercial and recreational use.\n- The St. Johns River is 310 miles long and winds through or borders twelve counties, including three of Florida's largest counties.\n- The Astor Bridge is a single-leaf bascule bridge in Astor, Florida.\n- The Astor Bridge carries State Road 40 over the St. Johns River.",
